== Mentoring

I advise PhD students in the Department of Mathematics at NC State and mentor undergraduate researchers through NC State's [https://gti.ncsu.edu/gears/ GEARS] program (Global Training Initiative), which brings international undergraduates to Raleigh for a six-week research experience.

=== PhD students

- Arnel Smith (since 2024)
- Elly Do (since 2024)
- Harshit Bhatt (since 2024)

=== Undergraduate research

*2026 Summer GEARS* (July 6 to August 13, 2026)

- Jiaying Ye (University of Sheffield). Compression of image and text embeddings for cross-modal retrieval. Her paper /Validation-to-Test Transfer of Post-Hoc Compression for Efficient Vision-Language Retrieval/ (J. Ye and C. Chen) was accepted at [https://www.ieee-etecom.org IEEE ETECOM 2026].
- Junxiang Huang (The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen). Numerical stability of orthogonalization algorithms.
- Zhenhui Yuan (Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University). Worst-case error in low-rank matrix completion.
- Fengyu Zou (Duke Kunshan University). Similarity kernels in a data-driven method.

*2026 Winter GEARS* (online)

- Yu Li (University of Nottingham Ningbo China) and Xiangzhe Wang (The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen). Project: /Adaptive Stopping Rule for Power Iteration in Randomized SVD/. *First place*, 2026 Winter GEARS poster competition.

=== Earlier

